# "You may cast the exiled card" lets the card be cast as its Adventure too (CR 715.3, 601.3), and mana of any type pays for that
# spell (CR 609.4b). Bot1's Null Summoner exiles Bot2's Bonecrusher Giant, and Brain Freeze mills Bot1 to threshold. On turn
# three Bot1 casts Stomp from exile with Mox Jet and Mox Sapphire - no red - and Stomp deals 2 damage to Bot2. Stomp resolves
# and its controller, Bot1, exiles it on an adventure: "for as long as that card remains exiled, that player may play it"
# (CR 715.3d), though Bot2 owns it. That cast is the card's own new permission, not the Summoner's (the card is a new object,
# CR 400.7), so mana of any type no longer pays: with two Islands and Mox Pearl open the Giant's {2}{R} can't be paid. On
# turn five Mox Ruby pays its {R} and Bot1 casts Bonecrusher Giant, which it controls.

